  "body": "**Link to problem area**: https://spec.matrix.org/v1.2/#legacy-versioning\r\n\r\n**Issue**\r\nThe above clarifies a support matrix for backwards definition linking as \"v1.0 support\", however, it does little to define how to actually detect such v1.0 support.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/ruma/ruma/issues/852 raises some questions about this;\r\n- Should v1.0 be determined to be supported if any of the above revisions appear in `/versions`?\r\n  - Should it only be if *all* are detected?\r\n  - Should it be only on `r0.6.1` or `r0.6.0`?\r\n  - Should it be on *any* `r*` version?\r\n- Should it (additionally) also be determined if a server sends a `v1.0` string in there?\r\n",
